# TypeScript conventions (this repo)

## Documentation sources (prefer in order)

1. **Context7 MCP** — in `.cursor/mcp.json`. For TypeScript language questions:
   - `resolve-library-id` with query like "TypeScript handbook"
   - `get-library-docs` with `/microsoft/typescript` (optionally `topic`: generics, modules, tsconfig, etc.)
2. **Official handbook** — https://www.typescriptlang.org/docs/handbook/intro
3. **TSConfig reference** — https://www.typescriptlang.org/tsconfig/
4. **Context7 llms bundle** — https://context7.com/microsoft/TypeScript/llms.txt

There is no official `typescriptlang.org/llms.txt`; use Context7 or the handbook.

## Validate changes

Run `pnpm check` after non-trivial TypeScript edits (uses `svelte-check` + strict `tsconfig.json`).

## Project config

- **Strict mode** enabled (`strict: true`)
- **Module resolution**: `bundler` (SvelteKit/Vite)
- **Node types**: `@types/node` for server code (`src/lib/server/**`)
- **Path aliases**: `$lib`, `$app/*` from SvelteKit generated tsconfig

## Patterns for this codebase

```ts
// Prefer explicit types on public/server boundaries
export type FindMixesInput = { artists: { spotifyId: string; name: string }[] };

// SvelteKit server loads — import generated types
import type { PageServerLoad } from './$types';
import type { RequestHandler } from './$types';

// App locals — extend in src/app.d.ts, use event.locals.session
```

- Use `import type { ... }` for type-only imports
- Avoid `any`; prefer `unknown` + narrowing for external JSON
- Server secrets via `$env/dynamic/private`, not `process.env` in client code
- Shared types live in `src/lib/types/`; server logic in `src/lib/server/`

## Common pitfalls

- Don't use browser APIs in `+page.server.ts`, `+server.ts`, or `src/lib/server/**`
- `$lib/server/**` must not be imported from client components (SvelteKit enforces server-only)
- When Spotify/Mixcloud JSON is untyped, define minimal interfaces in `src/lib/types/`
